1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:16,040
I fell asleep, holding a precious jewel in my hand.

2
00:00:17,260 --> 00:00:21,060
The day was warm, with a gentle breeze.

3
00:00:22,420 --> 00:00:26,340
Now, I said, I have nothing to lose.

4
00:00:26,340 --> 00:00:37,520
Then, I woke up and scolded my foolish hand, for the jewel was gone.

5
00:00:39,480 --> 00:00:47,140
All I have left now are memories of an amethyst.

6
00:00:56,340 --> 00:01:02,020
Ui, is the past that important?

7
00:01:06,020 --> 00:01:11,520
Ui said, no matter how small, all her memories were important.

8
00:01:11,520 --> 00:01:15,460
If she lost even one, she'd be sad.

9
00:01:15,460 --> 00:01:28,560
Back then, this hospital room was all we had.

10
00:01:28,560 --> 00:01:30,760
Our own little world.

11
00:01:31,600 --> 00:01:36,820
The only thing keeping us connected to the outside, was Ui's sister, Iroha.

12
00:01:36,820 --> 00:01:46,780
It was all we needed, and we were happy.

13
00:01:46,780 --> 00:01:59,180
Hello, Iroha Tamaki.

14
00:02:00,460 --> 00:02:02,900
I can grant you any wish you desire.

15
00:02:06,200 --> 00:02:07,220
Any wish?

16
00:02:07,220 --> 00:02:13,520
One of these days, we should all go to a theme park.

17
00:02:13,980 --> 00:02:14,980
That reminds me.

18
00:02:15,260 --> 00:02:18,160
They were building one in Daito Ward, but never finished it.

19
00:02:18,900 --> 00:02:19,820
Oh, I know.

20
00:02:20,120 --> 00:02:22,140
Let's come up with a rumor about that place.

21
00:02:22,580 --> 00:02:25,080
Like, it's a happy place where angels hang out.

22
00:02:25,540 --> 00:02:28,860
How about, we call it the rumor of Kilation Land?

23
00:02:29,360 --> 00:02:33,160
Oh, and that play we did that Nemu wrote, could also be a neat rumor.

24
00:02:33,160 --> 00:02:35,340
The rumor of Good Fortune Water.

25
00:02:35,800 --> 00:02:38,080
And that place we had that bad argument?

26
00:02:38,860 --> 00:02:40,240
The friendship-ending staircase.

27
00:02:41,340 --> 00:02:43,800
You're not doing homework now, are you?

28
00:02:44,040 --> 00:02:44,820
Uh-uh, sis.

29
00:02:45,120 --> 00:02:49,040
We're making up urban legends, and we're planting them all over Kamehama.

30
00:02:50,040 --> 00:02:53,320
We thought, if we filled the city with our rumors...

31
00:02:53,320 --> 00:02:55,320
Then, after we died...

32
00:02:55,320 --> 00:02:58,980
Whenever you'd come across one of them, it would get you to remember us.

33
00:03:03,160 --> 00:03:07,200
It's a neat idea.

34
00:03:07,660 --> 00:03:08,680
Can I make one, too?

35
00:03:09,220 --> 00:03:09,700
Sure!

36
00:03:11,440 --> 00:03:14,100
Somewhere in the city, there's a bare Sakura tree.

37
00:03:14,560 --> 00:03:17,240
When the three girls are well again, and are out of the hospital,

38
00:03:17,620 --> 00:03:19,700
they'll go there and, under its branches,

39
00:03:20,220 --> 00:03:22,860
reunite with the girl who always came to visit them.

40
00:03:23,280 --> 00:03:26,500
On that day, the tree will bloom with the prettiest flowers.

41
00:03:26,940 --> 00:03:28,740
And it'll never be bare again.

42
00:03:29,120 --> 00:03:30,260
Now, to invoke it!

43
00:03:30,260 --> 00:03:38,280
This reunion, no matter how long it takes, will make the tree bloom.

44
00:03:39,280 --> 00:03:41,280
And the name of this tree will be...

45
00:03:42,500 --> 00:03:44,020
Rumor of the Eternal Sakura!

46
00:03:44,020 --> 00:04:00,900
Have you thought about my offer from the other day?

47
00:04:03,420 --> 00:04:05,600
It's hard to believe, to be honest.

48
00:04:06,600 --> 00:04:08,600
You humans only believe what you see.

49
00:04:08,900 --> 00:04:10,120
It's such a shame.

50
00:04:10,120 --> 00:04:22,040
Where's Ui?

51
00:04:25,340 --> 00:04:26,060
Ui!

52
00:04:34,060 --> 00:04:35,320
Oh, hi, sis.

53
00:04:35,320 --> 00:04:38,400
Thanks for coming out here so quickly.

54
00:04:41,620 --> 00:04:43,980
I'll rush over any time you need me to.

55
00:04:44,800 --> 00:04:46,760
I am your big sister, after all.

56
00:04:48,840 --> 00:04:51,200
It's good they stabilized you in time.

57
00:04:51,540 --> 00:04:53,480
For a second there, you had me worried.

58
00:04:54,360 --> 00:04:57,340
The doctor said I can't eat the lunches you bring.

59
00:04:57,680 --> 00:04:59,180
Not till I get better, anyway.

60
00:05:00,260 --> 00:05:03,780
You'll be better soon, and then I'll get to stuff you with my lunches.

61
00:05:03,780 --> 00:05:05,860
Bye.

62
00:05:22,440 --> 00:05:22,540
Bye!

63
00:05:22,600 --> 00:05:23,260
Bye!

64
00:05:23,340 --> 00:05:25,400
Bye!

65
00:05:26,740 --> 00:05:27,240
Bye!

66
00:05:27,240 --> 00:05:27,360
Bye!

67
00:05:27,720 --> 00:05:27,780
Bye!

68
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:31,420
Bye!

69
00:05:31,560 --> 00:05:31,740
Bye!

70
00:05:31,960 --> 00:05:32,620
Bye!

71
00:05:32,620 --> 00:05:33,560
Bye!

72
00:05:33,560 --> 00:05:33,580
Bye!

73
00:05:33,580 --> 00:05:33,760
Bye!

74
00:05:33,760 --> 00:05:43,100
Iroha! Did you hear? The doctor said I might get to leave soon!

75
00:05:46,420 --> 00:05:49,680
You should have seen the doctor's faces when they told her.

76
00:05:50,020 --> 00:05:52,660
They couldn't believe it. They said it was like magic.

77
00:05:53,080 --> 00:05:55,200
I guess miracles are real after all.

78
00:06:03,760 --> 00:06:05,680
D.R.I.N.S.

79
00:06:06,680 --> 00:06:18,940
Well, that sucks.

80
00:06:20,080 --> 00:06:25,200
Yeah. What's up? She's been acting kind of weird lately, hasn't she?

81
00:06:25,940 --> 00:06:30,560
She's not coming as often, and when she does, she seems really tired.

82
00:06:31,000 --> 00:06:34,680
It's like Uli's getting better, but now she's getting sick.

83
00:06:42,200 --> 00:06:44,560
Yeah, that shade's definitely the right one.

84
00:06:45,140 --> 00:06:46,460
You look super cute.

85
00:06:47,680 --> 00:06:49,780
It makes me look a little more grown up.

86
00:06:56,080 --> 00:06:57,920
Thanks, sis. I...

87
00:06:57,920 --> 00:06:59,680
Sorry, there's something I have to do.

88
00:07:00,560 --> 00:07:20,660
What could she have to do down here?

89
00:07:20,660 --> 00:07:30,860
What is all this?

90
00:07:31,320 --> 00:07:32,980
This place is unreal.

91
00:07:33,280 --> 00:07:34,160
Where's Iroha?

92
00:07:34,160 --> 00:07:51,280
Oh my gosh! That thing's trying to kill her!

93
00:07:51,480 --> 00:07:53,240
You can save her, if you want.

94
00:07:53,660 --> 00:07:55,800
I can give you the power to save her.

95
00:07:56,200 --> 00:07:58,860
But first, you have to make a contract with me.

96
00:07:58,860 --> 00:08:00,620
A contract?

97
00:08:00,620 --> 00:08:00,960
A contract?

98
00:08:00,960 --> 00:08:12,760
How's is this place?

99
00:08:12,920 --> 00:08:15,720
I don't know if you have to deal with him.

100
00:08:15,960 --> 00:08:18,140
What should you do with this place?

101
00:08:18,720 --> 00:08:19,680
What's if this is true?

102
00:08:19,680 --> 00:08:21,680
Irohatamaki

103
00:08:49,680 --> 00:09:01,320
If what Kyubei said is the truth, then the reason Irohat became a magical girl was to cure you

104
00:09:01,320 --> 00:09:05,240
But I don't want my sister to suffer because of me

105
00:09:05,240 --> 00:09:07,200
She doesn't deserve that

106
00:09:07,200 --> 00:09:12,100
Maybe if we make a contract with Kyubei and become magical girls too, we can save her

107
00:09:12,100 --> 00:09:13,620
Take it easy, Ui

108
00:09:13,620 --> 00:09:17,860
I don't trust what it told us, so we should proceed with caution

109
00:09:17,860 --> 00:09:18,940
I'm with her

110
00:09:18,940 --> 00:09:22,140
Besides, we don't know anything about magical girls anyway

111
00:09:22,140 --> 00:09:23,800
We should research it

112
00:09:23,800 --> 00:09:27,420
We'll have a better chance of saving your sister if we know what we're dealing with

113
00:09:27,420 --> 00:09:36,500
It won't take us long if we work together, so don't worry

114
00:09:36,500 --> 00:09:38,060
We'll save her

115
00:09:38,060 --> 00:09:41,960
Yeah, together we can do anything

116
00:09:41,960 --> 00:09:47,120
We believed there would be a happy ending

117
00:09:47,120 --> 00:09:50,320
We couldn't have been more naive

118
00:09:50,320 --> 00:10:03,880
Why are you researching witches?

119
00:10:04,340 --> 00:10:08,560
If I can figure out a more efficient way to get rid of them, you know, like all at once

120
00:10:08,560 --> 00:10:11,280
It would make the job easier for magical girls

121
00:10:11,280 --> 00:10:15,840
With that idea in mind, the wishes we picked should be ones that kill witches

122
00:10:15,840 --> 00:10:22,600
Based on what I discovered, witches attack humans, so we should investigate missing person cases in the city

123
00:10:22,600 --> 00:10:27,460
Here's what I found so far

124
00:10:27,460 --> 00:10:30,660
The blue dots are the last location of missing persons

125
00:10:30,660 --> 00:10:32,660
The red dots are where suicides happened

126
00:10:32,660 --> 00:10:36,100
Almost all of them seem to occur in clusters

127
00:10:36,100 --> 00:10:41,540
Yep, and if you add all the disasters and accidents that were likely caused by witches

128
00:10:41,540 --> 00:10:44,660
And then line up the deaths chronologically

129
00:10:44,660 --> 00:10:50,020
The first victim is always a young girl

130
00:10:50,020 --> 00:10:54,200
That means there's a connection between witches appearing and girls disappearing

131
00:10:54,200 --> 00:10:58,560
It's possible the first victims were magical girls who lost to witches

132
00:10:58,560 --> 00:11:02,700
That could explain the amount of mysterious sudden deaths

133
00:11:02,700 --> 00:11:07,040
Next up, let's go talk to an expert on the situation

134
00:11:07,040 --> 00:11:11,360
Okay, I'm here

135
00:11:11,360 --> 00:11:13,080
What did you want to ask me?

136
00:11:14,240 --> 00:11:17,460
Oh, uh, you promised to tell us the truth?

137
00:11:17,900 --> 00:11:18,760
Of course I will

138
00:11:18,760 --> 00:11:20,040
I don't lie

139
00:11:20,040 --> 00:11:22,520
Okay, then, um

140
00:11:22,520 --> 00:11:25,200
What's the reason you do what you do?

141
00:11:25,980 --> 00:11:29,380
Simply put, my goal is to extend the life of the universe

142
00:11:29,380 --> 00:11:32,280
Oh, and how do you do that?

143
00:11:33,280 --> 00:11:37,000
I collect and transform energy, then send it out to the universe

144
00:11:37,000 --> 00:11:39,620
What exactly is a witch anyway?

145
00:11:39,620 --> 00:11:41,580
Negative emotions manifested

146
00:11:41,580 --> 00:11:42,980
What's a soul gem?

147
00:11:43,360 --> 00:11:44,840
The soul of a magical girl

148
00:11:44,840 --> 00:11:46,160
That sounds important

149
00:11:46,160 --> 00:11:47,700
So do you make them?

150
00:11:48,120 --> 00:11:51,240
It's more like I take your energy and give it a physical form

151
00:11:51,240 --> 00:11:53,380
What did my sister pick up in the morgue?

152
00:11:53,620 --> 00:11:54,480
A grief seed

153
00:11:54,480 --> 00:11:56,860
After she picked it up, what did she do with it?

154
00:11:56,940 --> 00:11:58,060
Purified her soul gem

155
00:11:58,060 --> 00:11:58,500
Why?

156
00:11:58,760 --> 00:12:01,220
The more magic you use, the more tainted they become

157
00:12:01,220 --> 00:12:03,080
What happens if you don't purify them?

158
00:12:03,200 --> 00:12:05,140
You won't be able to use your magic properly

159
00:12:05,140 --> 00:12:07,360
Any more questions?

160
00:12:07,360 --> 00:12:09,440
One more, please

161
00:12:09,440 --> 00:12:10,980
If all witches vanished

162
00:12:10,980 --> 00:12:11,820
Would my sister

163
00:12:11,820 --> 00:12:12,720
I mean

164
00:12:12,720 --> 00:12:15,440
Would magical girls

165
00:12:15,440 --> 00:12:17,280
Have normal lives again?

166
00:12:18,320 --> 00:12:20,240
Their fates are intertwined

167
00:12:20,240 --> 00:12:21,980
If there were no more witches

168
00:12:21,980 --> 00:12:24,500
Then there could be no more magical girls either

169
00:12:24,500 --> 00:12:25,580
You see

170
00:12:25,580 --> 00:12:27,620
The only way to get grief seeds

171
00:12:27,620 --> 00:12:29,000
Is to defeat witches

172
00:12:29,000 --> 00:12:35,240
You stupid machine

173
00:12:35,240 --> 00:12:46,640
I'm even more confused now than I was before

174
00:12:46,640 --> 00:12:48,980
We learned a lot though

175
00:12:48,980 --> 00:12:51,540
We know what Cube A's role in all this is

176
00:12:51,540 --> 00:12:53,760
And as for the truth behind magical girls

177
00:12:53,760 --> 00:12:55,360
It's easy to guess that

178
00:12:55,360 --> 00:12:57,040
